{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"appealing-driveable-ass","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n`_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`, about line 625) runs `_apply_review_floors` only when `engine == \"pipeline\"`. Under the agentic engine, these steps are skipped:\n- the Pass-3 rising floor;\n- the completion floor;\n- the drift floor (`drift_floor.maybe_apply`, which can downgrade BLOCK to PASS through `_recompute_verdict_after_drop`);\n- the consistency cross-checks (`xcheck.maybe_apply_contradiction` and `maybe_apply_comment_trail`, which rewrite `verdict[\"blocking\"]`);\n- fix-unit grouping.\n\nSo for the same plan material and findings, the two engines can sign different verdict strings and blocking lists.\n\nThe code comment cites ADR 0123, but `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md` documents only the Layer-1 floor and claimability running first under both engines. It does not say that the post-dispatch tail is pipeline-only, or that the drift floor's convergence (a code-drift re-review of an unchanged plan converging back to PASS) does not apply to agentic reviews.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Either the tail steps that change the verdict string or the `blocking` list (the drift floor and the cross-checks) also run on agentic verdicts, or ADR 0123 is amended to state and justify that they are pipeline-only.\n- [ ] A test pins the chosen behavior under both engines.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"5bd7-33ec-8630-440e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Agentic verdicts skip drift floor and cross-checks"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794547697775543001,"uuid":"c6edfec9-92b5-4372-9d87-cd9dc30ff706"}